```
Confirmed absent: `grep fiscal` over `src/main` returns nothing; `openapi.yml` has no `fiscalYear`; there is no `OwnerDto.java` source (it is generated by the openapi-generator-maven-plugin from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`). To surface a `fiscalYear` field you would add it to `openapi.yml`, add a `@Mapping(target="fiscalYear", ...)` + default method in `OwnerMapper`, basing it on `getRegistrationDate()`.

## 1. Membership identifier (membership ID with year segment)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipNumber.java` — assigns `membershipNumber` as `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the registrationDate year:
```java
18  public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
19      String yy = String.format("%02d", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);
20      owner.setMembershipNumber(owner.getCustomerCode() + "-M" + yy);
21  }
```
This is the clearest precedent for the fiscal-year task: it already derives a `<prefix><2-digit-year>` string from `registrationDate.getYear()`. Note the YY format `%02d` vs. the test's expected `FY\d{2}` format.

Stored on the model: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java:76-77` (`@Column(name = "membership_number") private String membershipNumber;`), getter/setter at lines 191-196.

OpenAPI doc: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml:2232-2240` describes `membershipNumber` format `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'`, example `'SYD-SMI-0007-M26'`.

The `customerCode` prefix comes from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java` (delegates to `OwnerCustomerCode.of(owner)`, region-and-hash identity).

## 2. Tenure (counting years / 365-day window)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`
```java
172  /** The owner's tenure in whole days: ... from registrationDate to today. Returns 0 when no
173      registration date is stored (or it lies in the future) ... */
177  default long tenureDays(Owner owner) {
178      java.time.LocalDate registrationDate = owner.getRegistrationDate();
179      if (registrationDate == null) { return 0; }
182      long days = java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, java.time.LocalDate.now());
183      return Math.max(days, 0);
184  }
```
Used by `membershipPoints` (lines 137-152): `+3` points when `tenureDays(owner) > 365`:
```java
148      if (tenureDays(owner) > 365) { points += 3; }
```
`membershipLevel` (158-170) buckets the points 1-4. Both are wired into the DTO via `@Mapping` expressions in the mapper interface header (lines 28-29). OpenAPI doc of these: `openapi.yml:2241-2261` ("+3 for tenure over 365 days").

Related date-window logic: `ageBand` (OwnerMapper.java:69-84) computes age in years with `Period.between(birthDate, asOf)` where `asOf` is the registrationDate (fallback to now).

## 3. Business-day-adjusted registration date
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BusinessDay.java` — the single source of truth:
```java
25  private static final Set<LocalDate> HOLIDAYS = Set.of(
