53  static long countOwnersOn(LocalDate businessDay, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) { ... }
```
Rolls weekends/holidays forward to the next business day; `countOwnersOn` is shared by the daily-limit and bulk-signup rules.

Applied in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java:13-20`: defaults a null registrationDate to `LocalDate.now()`, then `owner.setRegistrationDate(BusinessDay.rollForward(effective))`. The Javadoc explicitly says everything derived from it (e.g. the membership number's year segment) reads this adjusted value — so a fiscalYear derivation should also read the already-adjusted stored `registrationDate`.

Tests replicate this with `toBusinessDay(...)` and the same HOLIDAYS set in `AcceptanceBase.java:239-274`.

## 4. Registration date handling (validation + default)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate.java` — rejects a future registrationDate (only when present) with `FutureRegistrationDateException`; null is allowed (defaulted later):
```java
17  public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request) throws FutureRegistrationDateException {
18      LocalDate registrationDate = request.getRegistrationDate();
19      if (registrationDate != null && registrationDate.isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {
20          throw new FutureRegistrationDateException(registrationDate);
21      }
22  }
```
Supporting classes in same package: `FutureRegistrationDateException.java`, and handler `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler.java`.

Model field: `Owner.java:67-68` `@Column(name = "registration_date", columnDefinition = "DATE") private LocalDate registrationDate;`, getter/setter lines 167-173.

## Pipeline order (where to hook fiscalYear)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` defines the `POST /api/owners` orchestration. Relevant order: `validateRegistrationDate` (line 12) → ... → `build` (BuildOwner, line 36, rolls to business day) → ... → `assignMembershipNumber` (line 61) → ... → `save` → `audit` → `respond`. So by the time it is stored, `registrationDate` is business-day-adjusted. `fiscalYear`, being a read-time derived value like `membershipPoints`/`tenureDays`, would most naturally be an `OwnerMapper` default method + `@Mapping`, not a pipeline function.

## Tests
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — the only concrete test; asserts `fiscalYear` matches `FY\d{2}` (currently will fail — unimplemented).
